# T5. A skill file edited by hand to break the limits is refused skill_invalid and latches skill_invalid, both
# when it is asked for and when it was edited after the walker asked (it is read again at the press):
# - one waypoint 40° from the last (over its 30°/s): fails SkillSchema;
# - the wrist turned to 95° throughout: passes SkillSchema, fails checkSkillAgainstSetup (outside the calibrated
#   range less the margin).
# Put back, it is asked about again.
expect motion mode ready
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key pose-ready-left
wait 2100
key c
expect 5000 motion command arm.go_to_pose completed operator_cli
key skill-edit-too-fast
key skill-run-sample
expect motion command skill.run refused:skill_invalid operator_cli
expect motion fault skill_invalid system
expect motion mode fault
key operator-clear
wait 2100
key c
expect motion cleared all faults
key skill-edit-out-of-range
key skill-run-sample
expect motion command skill.run refused:skill_invalid operator_cli
expect motion fault skill_invalid system
key operator-clear
wait 2100
key c
expect motion cleared all faults
# Asked about while valid, edited before the press: refused at the press, and nothing moves.
key skill-restore-sample
key skill-run-sample
expect motion target skill.run operator_cli: SIMULATED sample: hold it out
key skill-edit-too-fast
wait 2100
key c
expect motion command skill.run refused:skill_invalid operator_cli
expect motion fault skill_invalid system
absent 1000 motion skill.run started
key operator-clear
wait 2100
key c
expect motion cleared all faults
key skill-restore-sample
key skill-run-sample
expect motion target skill.run operator_cli: SIMULATED sample: hold it out
key q
